#
# Local url:
URL='http://localhost:9000'

# IMGIX:
# By default, imgix is disabled locally. Uncomment the following line to view images through imgix:
# USE_IMGIX=true
#
# GitHub:
# If you'd like to see live GitHub data in /members or the sponsors section, you'll need a token from github
# https://docs.github.com/en/github/authenticating-to-github/creating-a-personal-access-token
# The token does not need any permissions, so you can leave all of the "scope" boxes unchecked.
# One you have your token, uncomment the following line and add your token
# GITHUB_TOKEN=yourtoken
#
# CMS:
# If you'd like to see live CMS data, you'll need to ask a maintainer for a CMS token. Once you have that,
# add your token and uncomment the following two lines:
#
# CMS_URL='https://members.virtualcoffee.io'
# CMS_TOKEN=cmstoken
#
# Redirect handlers (/join-coffee in netlify/functions/, /join-slack in src/app/join-slack/):
#
# Only needed if you're working on those functions locally — production values live in
# Netlify's env settings.
#
# SLACK_JOIN_LINK=https://join.slack.com/t/...
# ZOOM_TUESDAYS=https://zoom.us/j/...
# ZOOM_THURSDAYS=https://zoom.us/j/...
#
# Bot blocking (/netlify/edge-functions/block-bots.ts):
#
# The blocklist is skipped in local dev. Uncomment to exercise it against
# localhost — deployed environments always enforce it regardless of this value.
#
# BLOCK_BOTS_LOCAL=true
##
# ── Membership database and /admin ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The database itself needs no configuration: `netlify dev` starts a local
# Postgres and @netlify/database finds it. Run `pnpm db:migrate` once, then
# `pnpm db:seed` for realistic sample applications.
#
# /admin normally requires signing in with Slack. Contributors without those
# credentials can set this to explore it locally — it is ignored in every
# deployed environment:
#
# ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS=true
#
# By default the bypass session is a full admin. Set this to exercise the
# narrower roles — the value is the same comma-separated string stored in
# user.role (see src/lib/permissions.ts):
#
# ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS_ROLES=volunteer_coordinator
#
# `volunteer` is a role like any other here, and gets you into /invites rather
# than /admin — it grants no admin section at all, on purpose (docs/adr/0010).
# An Invite Allowance is keyed on the Slack member id, so the bypass session
# carries one; it defaults to U_DEV_BYPASS, which is the Volunteer `pnpm
# db:seed` creates. Override it to act as a different one:
#
# ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS_SLACK_ID=U_DEV_BYPASS
#
# The deploy-preview equivalent, PREVIEW_ADMIN_BYPASS (and
# PREVIEW_ADMIN_BYPASS_ROLES), unblocks /admin on a live preview URL instead —
# see docs/adr/0007. It only has any effect once Netlify sets
# CONTEXT=deploy-preview, so it belongs in the Netlify UI's deploy-preview
# context, not here.
#
# Slack OAuth (maintainers only). Create these on the vc-bots Slack app and
# register the redirect URI http://localhost:9000/api/auth/callback/slack.
# SLACK_TEAM_ID pins sign-in to the Virtual Coffee workspace.
#
# SLACK_CLIENT_ID=
# SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SLACK_TEAM_ID=T00000000
#
# Better Auth. The secret signs sessions; generate one with
# `openssl rand -base64 32`.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:9000
#
# Comma-separated Slack member ids that become admins the first time they sign
# in. This only bootstraps the first admin: after that, roles are granted and
# revoked in /admin, and someone who has not signed in yet gets a Pending Grant
# from the "Grant access" picker instead. Removing an id here revokes nothing.
#
# Find yours in Slack: your profile, then the ⋮ menu, "Copy member ID".
#
# ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_SLACK_IDS=U0123ABCDEF
#
# Transactional email, sent through Google Workspace as hello@virtualcoffee.io.
# The password is a Workspace App Password, not the account password.
#
# GOOGLE_SMTP_USER=hello@virtualcoffee.io
# GOOGLE_SMTP_APP_PASSWORD=
#
# Slack notifications for the four public forms. These replace the Airtable
# automations that used to post them. One incoming webhook per destination, so
# a missing one only silences its own form — create them on the vc-bots Slack
# app. Without them a submission is still saved, and the failure is recorded
# and shown on the /admin dashboard.
#
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_COC=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_VOLUNTEERS=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_LUNCH_AND_LEARN=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_COFFEE_TABLES=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
#
# The membership pipeline's own channel. Used when someone claims a volunteer
# invite, because that application jumps to the front of the waitlist:
#
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_MEMBERSHIP=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
#
# Bot token with the `users:read` scope, for the Slack member directory behind
# the "Grant access" picker in /admin/user-management. A different credential
# from SLACK_CLIENT_* above: sign-in only asks for OIDC scopes, which cannot
# call users.list. Without it the picker falls back to mock members.
#
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
#
# The GitHub App, for opening the Lunch & Learn issue in
# Virtual-Coffee/VC-Community-Docs. The App must be installed on that repo with
# the issues permission.
#
# Same App and same values as the CI_APP_* Actions secrets the workflows use —
# only the variable names differ between the two environments. This is not
# GITHUB_TOKEN above, which stays a permission-less read-only PAT.
#
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
#
# One-off Airtable imports and snapshots. Read keys, one per base. The runbook
# for all of these scripts is scripts/airtable/README.md — note that these scripts
# do not read this file, so the key goes on the command line.
#
# Membership base (`scripts/airtable/importMembership.ts`).
#
# MEMBERSHIP_AIRTABLE_API_KEY=token
#
# Public Data and Monthly Challenges bases
# (`scripts/airtable/snapshotChallenges.ts`). The challenge pages read committed
# JSON, so nothing needs this at runtime — it is only here so the snapshot can
# be regenerated.
#
# PUBLIC_AIRTABLE_API_KEY=token
#
# Form Submissions base (`scripts/airtable/importSubmissions.ts`).
#
# FORMS_AIRTABLE_API_KEY=token
#
# That import also stores four historical CoC attachments in Netlify Blobs.
# Locally there is nothing to set: scripts/with-local-netlify.ts supplies a
# store. Set these two only to write to the *production* store, which is what
# the real migration needs — they override the local one.
#
# NETLIFY_SITE_ID=
# NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN=
